        "by": "human",
        "reason": "Type B cast defect: TRY_TO_TIMESTAMP(REGEXP_REPLACE(col, offset-strip), \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss[.SSSSSS]\") returns NULL on any shape the pinned format misses (date-only values especially), and TRY_ makes it silent -- those NULLs reach the judge as differing_null_only/gap_shaped, i.e. a parse failure disguised as a FHIR coverage gap at the lower bar. Replace every datetime mapping with a bare TRY_CAST(col AS TIMESTAMP_NTZ). See pathling-sql SKILL.md and MIMIC_NOTES.md:337.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_justification": "The 197,931 only-oracle rows are the independently counted hospital POE/detail branch selected by General Care/Code status. The served FHIR warehouse has no resource/path carrying those POE events, poe_detail.field_value, or poe.ordertime. MedicationRequest's medication-request-poe identifier stream is a different medication/IV/TPN subset and was tested and rejected. The Observation chart branch is fully represented, and attempt 0002 completed Observation.id UUID-witness recovery for all nine prior timestamp substitutions, leaving 71,141 exact chart tuples and no candidate residual. No divergent dependencies exist.",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
      },
      {
