        "by": "human",
        "reason": "concept.sql hardcodes nine literal Observation UUIDs, each mapped to an oracle timestamp read from attempt_0001's divergence report. That is evaluation-fitted row identity, not a FHIR mapping, and sql_lint refuses it (hardcoded-resource-id). The omitted POE branch changes row inclusion and must be presented to the judge as essential representation loss, not automatically re-accepted as a partial table.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_justification": "The 197,931 only_oracle rows are an intrinsic row-level representation gap. Canonical mimic-iv/concepts/treatment/code_status.sql:36-65,67-77 unions ICU chart rows with hospital poe/poe_detail rows selected by poe.order_type='General Care' and poe.order_subtype='Code status'. The served MIMIC-on-FHIR warehouse has no resource or FHIR path preserving those hospital code-status POE events, poe.ordertime, or poe_detail.field_value. The nearest MedicationRequest.identifier.where(system='http://mimic.mit.edu/fhir/mimic/identifier/medication-request-poe').value stream is unrelated: its identifiers had zero intersection with selected code-status POE IDs, and authoredOn/status do not carry the missing payload. An independent full-data source count found exactly 197,931 selected POE/detail rows, matching the entire residual; the candidate's 71,141 chart rows have zero only_candidate rows, so the representable branch is exact. Every defensible mapping was tried: exact Observation system/code 223758, valueString, effective variants with TIMESTAMP_NTZ, identifier.value casts, ICU Encounter/partOf/hospital spine, and Observation.id timestamp-witness recovery. No divergent dependencies exist.",
